WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.730
A sheet of paper.

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:06.710
On it, a short program that marks
tests and prints Pass or Fail.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.210
The rule is simple: any mark
of 50 or more should pass.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.070
A student scored exactly 50.

5
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.850
Someone suspects the
program will fail them.

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.110
But there is no computer in the room.

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.050
So how could you prove there's
a bug before anyone types it in?

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.670
In this mission, you'll see the
same steps written two ways:

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.290
as a flowchart, and as pseudocode, which
isn't tied to one programming language.

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.090
And you'll meet a sneaky
kind of bug, a logic error:

11
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.050
the code runs, but gives a wrong result.

12
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.320
Your mission: find the
bug without pressing run.
